1
00:00:49,678 --> 00:00:51,722
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES, AND EVENTS
IN THIS WORK ARE FICTITIOUS

2
00:00:51,805 --> 00:00:53,432
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

3
00:01:43,398 --> 00:01:44,483
Boss.

4
00:01:47,444 --> 00:01:48,445
That really hurts.

5
00:01:48,946 --> 00:01:51,073
So that's what love does to people.

6
00:01:51,698 --> 00:01:55,160
You really got that fired up
over a few insults?

7
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:59,206
Just out of curiosity

8
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:03,127
did you really think
you could take those guys?

9
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,672
I just wanted to get my ass kicked.
Hard enough to knock my senses out.

10
00:02:07,881 --> 00:02:09,591
You're a pervert, aren't you?

11
00:02:11,802 --> 00:02:13,220
You're totally my type.

12
00:02:31,947 --> 00:02:35,909
NEWSHOUND HEE-KOOK

13
00:02:37,452 --> 00:02:39,454
What's going on
between Ah-jin and In-gang?

14
00:02:39,538 --> 00:02:40,539
Did you call for a driver?

15
00:02:42,541 --> 00:02:45,377
They were making out.
Did he dump you for her?

16
00:02:47,504 --> 00:02:49,173
Lena, are you there?

17
00:02:49,965 --> 00:02:51,175
Are you in shock?

18
00:03:27,628 --> 00:03:28,629
Be careful.

19
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:33,133
Lena's cousin, reporter Lim Hee-kook,
knows about you and In-gang.

20
00:03:49,149 --> 00:03:54,071
EPISODE 7: THE WHEEL OF FATE

21
00:03:55,447 --> 00:03:58,450
Do you know how damaging
a scandal like this can be for you?

22
00:03:59,451 --> 00:04:03,830
I'll try to keep the press at bay,
but you need to end things with him.

23
00:04:04,831 --> 00:04:06,250
It's better to end it now

24
00:04:06,333 --> 00:04:08,669
than let a messy relationship
make things awkward at work.

25
00:04:09,795 --> 00:04:10,796
Ms. Seo.

26
00:04:11,964 --> 00:04:14,633
This isn't some casual fling.

27
00:04:15,217 --> 00:04:17,010
We really like each other.

28
00:04:17,094 --> 00:04:18,095
Are you joking?

29
00:04:19,221 --> 00:04:21,890
You're a smart girl,
so stop acting like you don't get it.

30
00:04:22,224 --> 00:04:24,518
This isn't the right time
for you to be dating.

31
00:04:25,727 --> 00:04:28,647
Did you get this photo
from Lim Hee-kook?

32
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:29,731
Why do you ask?

33
00:04:29,815 --> 00:04:31,108
I'll talk to him.

34
00:04:31,191 --> 00:04:33,068
He doesn't like you. You know that.

35
00:04:33,151 --> 00:04:35,529
If he reached out to you
before running the story

36
00:04:36,071 --> 00:04:37,656
he must be after something.

37
00:04:38,323 --> 00:04:40,867
I'd like to talk to him in person.

38
00:04:40,951 --> 00:04:42,494
What are you going to do?

39
00:04:42,577 --> 00:04:43,912
I'll hear him out

40
00:04:44,788 --> 00:04:46,873
and if the terms are acceptable,
I'll cut a deal.

41
00:04:58,427 --> 00:05:01,596
I'll see myself out
so the two of you can talk.

42
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:20,324
What happened?

43
00:05:21,783 --> 00:05:25,370
You said yourself
you wanted nothing to do with her.

44
00:05:26,163 --> 00:05:27,956
I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

45
00:05:30,083 --> 00:05:31,543
I didn't expect this to happen.

46
00:05:31,835 --> 00:05:33,378
Forget about her for a second.

47
00:05:33,462 --> 00:05:36,131
Do you know how bad this scandal
will make you look?

48
00:05:36,214 --> 00:05:38,508
You just announced
your breakup with Lena.

49
00:05:38,592 --> 00:05:41,720
People will call it a rebound,
and you'll get slammed for it.

50
00:05:41,803 --> 00:05:43,847
Things like this
don't sit well with the public.

51
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:45,724
How are you going to handle that?

52
00:05:46,308 --> 00:05:47,309
Mi-ri.

53
00:05:48,602 --> 00:05:50,145
I'm no longer afraid of that.

54
00:05:51,355 --> 00:05:53,190
I'm not taking this lightly either.

55
00:05:54,775 --> 00:05:56,068
I'll take whatever comes.

56
00:05:56,902 --> 00:05:58,612
- You really--
- I'd really love it

57
00:05:59,154 --> 00:06:01,281
if you could give us your blessing.

58
00:06:03,075 --> 00:06:05,077
Give us your support.

59
00:06:08,038 --> 00:06:09,289
You'll do that, right?

60
00:06:27,015 --> 00:06:29,184
I heard you're good at your job

61
00:06:29,601 --> 00:06:31,311
so I wanted to treat you to a meal.

62
00:06:32,854 --> 00:06:36,274
You know how touchy folks are
about scandals these days.

63
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:39,903
He started dating you
the moment he broke up with Lena.

64
00:06:40,278 --> 00:06:44,699
That's the kind of thing
that can ruin a beloved actor.

65
00:06:46,701 --> 00:06:48,787
You're not very good
at making threats.

66
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:51,331
Save that speech for In-gang.

67
00:06:51,415 --> 00:06:54,167
I don't have much to lose
from this relationship.

68
00:06:54,876 --> 00:06:57,003
If anything,
it might even spark some curiosity.

69
00:06:57,087 --> 00:06:58,130
Fine.

70
00:06:58,797 --> 00:06:59,881
In that case

71
00:07:00,549 --> 00:07:03,343
I'll release this article as well.

72
00:07:07,055 --> 00:07:08,515
BAEK AH-JIN BECOMES
HEO IN-GANG'S GIRL

73
00:07:08,598 --> 00:07:12,352
Don't you think
that headline is a little tacky?

74
00:07:12,727 --> 00:07:14,604
- Excuse me?
- Change the headline

75
00:07:14,688 --> 00:07:17,023
to "Baek Ah-jin, the woman
who captured In-gang's heart."

76
00:07:20,402 --> 00:07:21,486
Listen, Ms. Baek.

77
00:07:22,904 --> 00:07:26,199
Mr. Lim, I hear you're Lena's cousin.

78
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,161
Cousins hang out when they're kids.

79
00:07:29,244 --> 00:07:31,246
And as adults,
exchange occasional texts.

80
00:07:31,329 --> 00:07:34,958
So why don't you leave it at that
and get friendly with me instead?

81
00:07:35,542 --> 00:07:36,918
I don't need friends.

82
00:07:37,836 --> 00:07:40,755
But I'm all ears
if you're offering something else.

83
00:07:40,839 --> 00:07:41,840
Do you mean money?

84
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:49,890
You're already getting a salary,
so I don't need to pad your pockets.

85
00:07:50,849 --> 00:07:52,642
You know how it is.

86
00:07:52,726 --> 00:07:56,271
People are always curious
about celebrity relationships.

87
00:07:56,688 --> 00:07:59,774
Someone else's love life
is always more entertaining.

88
00:07:59,858 --> 00:08:03,278
I was hoping you'd be the one
to write those entertaining pieces.

89
00:08:03,361 --> 00:08:05,489
So? What's the catch?

90
00:08:05,572 --> 00:08:08,366
If you accept my offer right now

91
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:13,413
I'll give you the exclusive rights
to our love story.

92
00:08:13,914 --> 00:08:16,708
Of course, this stays between us.

93
00:08:18,210 --> 00:08:21,421
You can use the photos
in this flash drive.

94
00:08:24,382 --> 00:08:27,469
Who took these photos?

95
00:08:27,552 --> 00:08:30,263
I'm giving them to you
so you don't have to tail me.

96
00:08:30,639 --> 00:08:32,516
And I'll keep them coming.

97
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:35,143
You won't regret this.

98
00:08:36,269 --> 00:08:37,771
I guarantee you

99
00:08:37,854 --> 00:08:41,566
that my love story will be fiery
and impossible to ignore.

100
00:08:42,442 --> 00:08:46,071
Rising star Baek Ah-jin
and actor Heo In-gang

101
00:08:46,154 --> 00:08:49,533
were spotted
on a private outing in Gangnam.

102
00:08:49,616 --> 00:08:53,495
As news of their blossoming romance
sweeps across the country

103
00:08:53,578 --> 00:08:55,872
fans appear split.

104
00:08:55,956 --> 00:08:59,751
Some are thrilled,
saying the two look perfect together.

105
00:08:59,834 --> 00:09:02,087
Others, however,
are criticizing the timing

106
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:05,340
accusing him of moving on too quickly
after his breakup with Lena.

107
00:09:05,423 --> 00:09:09,261
Whatever the truth may be,
it's a new beginning for the couple.

108
00:09:09,344 --> 00:09:13,139
So rather than dragging them down,
we should show them a little support.

109
00:09:18,687 --> 00:09:19,813
- Hyang-i.
- Yes?

110
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:22,816
- Are you going on a date today?
- No.

111
00:09:24,568 --> 00:09:26,695
Come on.
It's written all over your face.

112
00:09:27,612 --> 00:09:28,863
Is it a blind date?

113
00:09:28,947 --> 00:09:30,407
Something like that.

114
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,741
What time?

115
00:09:31,825 --> 00:09:32,826
It's at 7 p.m.

116
00:09:33,451 --> 00:09:34,452
Why do you ask?

117
00:09:35,036 --> 00:09:36,496
I'll let the salon know.

118
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:38,748
Get your hair done nicely
and have fun.

119
00:09:39,541 --> 00:09:41,626
Thank you so much, Ah-jin!

120
00:09:42,502 --> 00:09:45,005
- And don't drink too much.
- I won't.

121
00:09:45,088 --> 00:09:47,048
You get way too honest
when you drink.

122
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:48,675
Okay, I promise.

123
00:09:49,593 --> 00:09:50,594
I'll watch my mouth.

124
00:09:52,262 --> 00:09:54,306
Why are you so handsome?

125
00:09:55,807 --> 00:09:57,350
You're a manager

126
00:09:57,434 --> 00:10:00,103
so you must meet
a lot of good-looking celebrities.

127
00:10:00,186 --> 00:10:03,315
Being a manager
isn't all it's cracked up to be.

128
00:10:03,398 --> 00:10:06,735
You have no idea
how much dirt we have to deal with.

129
00:10:08,445 --> 00:10:10,739
Did you take the blame
for someone else's crime?

130
00:10:11,197 --> 00:10:12,407
How did you know that?

131
00:10:15,535 --> 00:10:17,912
No. You didn't hear it from me.

132
00:10:19,331 --> 00:10:20,498
Don't do that to me.

133
00:10:20,582 --> 00:10:22,334
I'll keep it to myself, so tell me.

134
00:10:22,417 --> 00:10:23,418
No.

135
00:10:29,549 --> 00:10:30,592
Hyang-i.

136
00:10:34,554 --> 00:10:37,223
Talking to someone can help you
get things off your chest.

137
00:10:38,141 --> 00:10:40,018
I promise I'll keep it a secret.

138
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:49,110
You can't tell anyone about this.

139
00:10:52,822 --> 00:10:55,575
A few years back...

140
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:27,065
- Hyang-i.
- Yes?

141
00:11:28,191 --> 00:11:29,401
Thanks for telling me.

142
00:11:30,568 --> 00:11:32,612
Don't tell anyone else.

143
00:11:36,908 --> 00:11:38,284
I'm supposed to take a break?

144
00:11:38,368 --> 00:11:40,995
- There must be scripts coming in.
- There are.

145
00:11:41,079 --> 00:11:45,875
But the other actors turn it down
when they find out you're the lead.

146
00:11:46,292 --> 00:11:47,335
You have to accept it.

147
00:11:47,419 --> 00:11:50,088
Who would want to work with
an actress who beat up a junior?

148
00:11:50,171 --> 00:11:51,339
Seriously.

149
00:11:51,756 --> 00:11:53,174
I slapped her once.

150
00:11:54,217 --> 00:11:55,218
Twice, tops.

151
00:11:55,844 --> 00:11:56,970
And I had my reasons.

152
00:11:57,303 --> 00:11:59,472
Do you know how she got back at me?

153
00:11:59,556 --> 00:12:01,349
You know how ruthless she is.

154
00:12:01,683 --> 00:12:02,892
What am I going to do with you?

155
00:12:03,601 --> 00:12:04,602
What's with that look?

156
00:12:04,936 --> 00:12:06,896
You still haven't come
to your senses.

157
00:12:08,565 --> 00:12:09,566
Get out of here.

158
00:12:29,878 --> 00:12:32,046
When Lena got caught driving drunk

159
00:12:33,131 --> 00:12:35,842
I covered for her
and said I was the one driving.

160
00:12:37,093 --> 00:12:38,428
I was even interrogated

161
00:12:38,511 --> 00:12:41,055
for supposedly
driving under the influence.

162
00:12:41,473 --> 00:12:42,474
Lena.

163
00:12:52,525 --> 00:12:53,985
Why do you look so surprised?

164
00:13:04,746 --> 00:13:06,331
Well, I warned you

165
00:13:07,665 --> 00:13:08,792
not to mess with me.

166
00:13:11,252 --> 00:13:12,629
Why won't you ever listen?

167
00:13:16,007 --> 00:13:18,718
It kind of kills the fun
if you're already making that face.

168
00:13:18,802 --> 00:13:22,013
Tell me you didn't
release this video yet.

169
00:13:23,890 --> 00:13:25,141
You didn't, right?

170
00:13:25,642 --> 00:13:26,643
Oh, dear.

171
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:30,605
Is that what you want to know?

172
00:13:30,688 --> 00:13:34,442
Please, Ah-jin.
If this goes public, I'm finished.

173
00:13:34,526 --> 00:13:36,194
You can take everything from me.

174
00:13:36,486 --> 00:13:37,612
Just help me.

175
00:13:39,197 --> 00:13:40,490
Who says you're finished?

176
00:13:44,577 --> 00:13:46,830
You're not.
This is just the beginning.

177
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:49,290
Hell doesn't end with a single blow.

178
00:14:06,850 --> 00:14:07,851
See?

179
00:14:08,351 --> 00:14:09,894
This won't be ending anytime soon.

180
00:14:15,525 --> 00:14:19,112
That's why you should've
listened to me.

181
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:24,325
I wouldn't have taken it this far
if you had left me alone.

182
00:14:27,203 --> 00:14:29,497
Don't ever think about
coming back to this business.

183
00:14:29,581 --> 00:14:31,082
And spare yourself the fantasy

184
00:14:31,165 --> 00:14:33,459
that you can disappear
for a few years and sneak back in.

185
00:14:33,710 --> 00:14:35,336
Don't beg me to save you either.

186
00:14:36,421 --> 00:14:37,714
Because I won't.

187
00:14:39,007 --> 00:14:40,925
Own it, Lena.

188
00:14:41,759 --> 00:14:44,012
Or let yourself crumble.

189
00:14:49,934 --> 00:14:50,935
No.

190
00:14:53,897 --> 00:14:54,898
What do I do?

191
00:15:20,381 --> 00:15:21,716
Did you see the video?

192
00:15:25,136 --> 00:15:27,639
This is all because you couldn't keep
your mouth shut.

193
00:15:29,682 --> 00:15:31,392
I told you to watch what you say.

194
00:15:34,103 --> 00:15:36,022
This isn't going to work between us.

195
00:15:36,773 --> 00:15:40,443
How am I supposed to trust you
after what you spilled?

196
00:15:41,486 --> 00:15:42,487
Wouldn't you agree?

197
00:15:45,365 --> 00:15:46,908
Consider today your last day.

198
00:15:49,661 --> 00:15:50,662
Ah-jin.

199
00:15:53,623 --> 00:15:56,626
- Happy birthday to you
- Happy birthday to you

200
00:15:56,709 --> 00:15:59,504
- Happy birthday to you
- Happy birthday to you

201
00:16:00,588 --> 00:16:01,673
HAPPY BIRTHDAY
HONG KYUNG-SUK

202
00:16:03,216 --> 00:16:05,885
This is my favorite color.

203
00:16:05,969 --> 00:16:07,470
I'm glad you like it.

204
00:16:07,553 --> 00:16:08,805
Thank you, Ah-jin.

205
00:16:09,472 --> 00:16:12,141
All right. One, two, three.

206
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:16,312
This has been such a lovely birthday.

207
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,491
WINTER SLEEP

208
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:57,937
How was your trip?

209
00:17:01,941 --> 00:17:04,110
HEO IN-GANG AND BAEK AH-JIN'S OUTFITS
AT THE AIRPORT

210
00:17:18,082 --> 00:17:21,044
HEO IN-GANG AND BAEK AH-JIN
ON SUMMER VACATION

211
00:17:46,819 --> 00:17:50,364
I'm deeply in love with her.

212
00:17:50,823 --> 00:17:52,658
So, I hope you guys understand.

213
00:17:52,742 --> 00:17:54,744
Show my Ah-jin some love.

214
00:17:54,827 --> 00:17:56,662
LIVE

215
00:18:20,353 --> 00:18:22,522
HEO IN-GANG AND BAEK AH-JIN
CAUGHT ON THE CUTEST DATE

216
00:18:22,605 --> 00:18:24,524
#LOVESTAGRAM #COUPLE
#BAEKGANG #COUPLEVIBES

217
00:18:34,117 --> 00:18:35,409
Were you writing again?

218
00:18:35,993 --> 00:18:37,411
I knew it.

219
00:18:37,870 --> 00:18:41,833
You obviously skipped breakfast.
Don't tell me you also skipped lunch.

220
00:18:42,458 --> 00:18:44,043
I brought you lunch just in case.

221
00:18:44,127 --> 00:18:46,629
I'm finishing up. You can eat first.

222
00:18:46,712 --> 00:18:48,506
Why don't you just join me?

223
00:18:49,257 --> 00:18:50,842
I bought this for you.

224
00:18:57,473 --> 00:18:58,474
Ta-da.

225
00:18:59,183 --> 00:19:00,184
Here.

226
00:19:02,228 --> 00:19:03,479
Are you busy tonight?

227
00:19:03,896 --> 00:19:04,981
No. Why?

228
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:08,484
Let's go to the premiere
of the movie Ah-jin is in.

229
00:19:11,028 --> 00:19:13,823
I just want to see if she's any good.

230
00:19:13,906 --> 00:19:15,783
I'll laugh at her if she's bad.

231
00:19:17,368 --> 00:19:18,369
Eat up.

232
00:19:26,043 --> 00:19:27,670
Hi, I'm Baek Ah-jin.

233
00:19:27,753 --> 00:19:29,255
VIP SCREENING
THE WOMAN WITH A SUITCASE

234
00:19:29,338 --> 00:19:32,049
I played Myo-hui.

235
00:19:32,133 --> 00:19:34,969
We had a lot of fun
filming this movie.

236
00:19:35,052 --> 00:19:40,099
Watching Myo-hui spiral into madness
should give you chills.

237
00:19:40,183 --> 00:19:42,435
Thank you for coming.
I hope you enjoy the movie.

238
00:19:42,518 --> 00:19:43,519
Thank you.

239
00:19:54,155 --> 00:19:56,824
THE WOMAN WITH A SUITCASE

240
00:20:10,463 --> 00:20:13,299
Jun-seo, you'll help me, right?

241
00:20:18,638 --> 00:20:20,139
Don't worry, Jun-seo.

242
00:20:22,225 --> 00:20:24,018
I'll date him for exactly a year.

243
00:20:27,939 --> 00:20:29,315
That's all I need.

244
00:20:39,325 --> 00:20:43,120
Reporters who saw the screening
are already writing their pieces

245
00:20:43,204 --> 00:20:44,622
and they're pretty favorable.

246
00:20:47,250 --> 00:20:48,668
I'm proud of you, Ah-jin.

247
00:21:00,096 --> 00:21:01,430
You smell nice.

248
00:21:02,014 --> 00:21:03,557
What cologne did you use today?

249
00:21:04,642 --> 00:21:06,978
I forgot to put any on.

250
00:21:10,481 --> 00:21:11,899
Then keep it that way.

251
00:21:13,150 --> 00:21:16,487
I like your natural scent
better than any cologne.

252
00:21:21,367 --> 00:21:22,827
I like you better than anything.

253
00:21:35,506 --> 00:21:39,176
Out gallivanting
instead of writing until this hour?

254
00:21:40,011 --> 00:21:43,723
Keep acting like a wife,
and I'll change the door code.

255
00:21:45,308 --> 00:21:47,935
Honey, what does "co-offender" mean?

256
00:21:48,019 --> 00:21:49,186
You don't need to know.

257
00:21:50,688 --> 00:21:51,939
I'll just look it up.

258
00:21:55,818 --> 00:21:58,904
"A person who, together with others,
directly carries out an act

259
00:21:58,988 --> 00:22:01,115
that satisfies the elements
of a criminal offense

260
00:22:01,198 --> 00:22:03,409
of the act itself"?

261
00:22:06,329 --> 00:22:08,289
Why the sudden interest in my book?

262
00:22:11,375 --> 00:22:13,544
I'm suddenly interested in you.

263
00:22:19,759 --> 00:22:22,636
Did Ah-jin call you?

264
00:22:23,054 --> 00:22:25,097
She doesn't call me nowadays.

265
00:22:28,517 --> 00:22:29,685
I guess she's happy.

266
00:22:35,441 --> 00:22:36,442
No.

267
00:22:36,901 --> 00:22:38,569
When the boss needs me

268
00:22:38,652 --> 00:22:41,530
it means something bad
has happened to her.

269
00:22:42,948 --> 00:22:44,325
So no news means good news.

270
00:22:45,242 --> 00:22:46,410
But...

271
00:22:54,668 --> 00:22:58,047
If I'm being honest,
I wish she would call me.

272
00:23:00,383 --> 00:23:01,467
I don't know.

273
00:23:05,054 --> 00:23:06,097
Want to grab a drink?

274
00:23:06,931 --> 00:23:07,932
No.

275
00:23:09,225 --> 00:23:10,393
Go home.

276
00:23:15,606 --> 00:23:17,817
I don't have a home.

277
00:23:18,275 --> 00:23:20,277
And if I leave, you'll die.

278
00:23:22,029 --> 00:23:23,239
Of boredom.

279
00:23:40,131 --> 00:23:42,049
MOM

280
00:23:42,925 --> 00:23:45,553
Pick up your phone. It's so loud.

281
00:23:46,178 --> 00:23:47,930
I'm trying to read here.

282
00:23:54,728 --> 00:23:56,230
Why won't you pick up?

283
00:23:59,191 --> 00:24:01,777
MOM

284
00:24:03,696 --> 00:24:04,697
Dude.

285
00:24:05,197 --> 00:24:06,907
You can't do that to your mother.

286
00:24:07,491 --> 00:24:10,161
How bad is it between you two
that you keep dodging her calls?

287
00:24:11,912 --> 00:24:13,372
You're a horrible son.

288
00:24:22,298 --> 00:24:24,341
Why aren't you answering my calls?

289
00:24:24,967 --> 00:24:26,927
The money you send me
is downright insulting.

290
00:24:32,892 --> 00:24:33,893
Jun-seo.

291
00:24:35,644 --> 00:24:36,937
I'll give you a week.

292
00:24:38,355 --> 00:24:40,274
Wire the money within a week.

293
00:24:52,077 --> 00:24:56,332
Don't let my mom know
about Grandpa's condition.

294
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,669
If she comes by, just send her away.

295
00:25:01,337 --> 00:25:03,339
Do you get what I'm saying?

296
00:25:04,340 --> 00:25:06,217
Yes, I do.

297
00:25:06,634 --> 00:25:08,052
Don't worry, Mr. Yoon.

298
00:25:26,487 --> 00:25:27,571
All done, ma'am.

299
00:25:29,281 --> 00:25:30,407
Thank you.

300
00:26:00,229 --> 00:26:02,147
INVESTMENT AGREEMENT

301
00:26:02,231 --> 00:26:03,691
LONGSTAR ENTERTAINMENT

302
00:26:16,495 --> 00:26:17,538
Did you put him up to it?

303
00:26:17,955 --> 00:26:20,082
You made him invest
in your company, didn't you?

304
00:26:20,958 --> 00:26:22,668
You haven't changed one bit.

305
00:26:23,586 --> 00:26:24,587
Doesn't it get tiring?

306
00:26:24,670 --> 00:26:26,755
You talked him into it.

307
00:26:26,839 --> 00:26:28,632
You only play the mother
because you're after

308
00:26:28,716 --> 00:26:30,050
your illegitimate
child's inheritance.

309
00:26:30,134 --> 00:26:31,677
So you have no right
to say that to me.

310
00:26:34,221 --> 00:26:36,140
That doesn't work on me anymore.

311
00:26:36,223 --> 00:26:38,392
So, you want Jun-seo to die.

312
00:26:39,393 --> 00:26:40,394
Don't you know

313
00:26:40,894 --> 00:26:44,315
how much he loves
his dad and grandpa?

314
00:26:45,232 --> 00:26:47,526
If he finds out
he isn't the biological son

315
00:26:47,610 --> 00:26:48,777
what do you think will happen?

316
00:26:50,404 --> 00:26:52,197
If you're set on destroying him

317
00:26:52,281 --> 00:26:53,949
be my guest.

318
00:26:57,077 --> 00:26:58,078
I'm sick of this.

319
00:27:06,587 --> 00:27:07,588
Hi.

320
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:12,635
Thank you.

321
00:27:13,677 --> 00:27:15,721
- Can we get a photo?
- Just one photo.

322
00:27:15,804 --> 00:27:16,805
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

323
00:27:18,432 --> 00:27:19,516
One, two, three.

324
00:27:22,227 --> 00:27:23,354
Don't cry.

325
00:27:24,813 --> 00:27:26,148
It's not over yet.

326
00:27:29,151 --> 00:27:31,028
You all need to know
what she really is!

327
00:27:31,111 --> 00:27:34,156
It was all her, you fucking idiots!

328
00:27:46,043 --> 00:27:49,672
You really thought
you could beat me, didn't you?

329
00:27:50,506 --> 00:27:54,343
Thank you for making my school life
so much less boring.

330
00:28:00,307 --> 00:28:02,893
I'm exposing
who Baek Ah-jin really is.

331
00:28:04,353 --> 00:28:07,439
We were classmates in 11th grade.

332
00:28:07,523 --> 00:28:09,525
She was the devil.

333
00:28:11,402 --> 00:28:14,655
She extorted money
from the other students at school.

334
00:28:15,114 --> 00:28:18,325
And she framed me for theft,
so I even had to transfer schools.

335
00:28:20,369 --> 00:28:24,790
What kind of messed-up world
lets someone like her be a celebrity?

336
00:28:25,416 --> 00:28:27,000
It's absurd.

337
00:28:28,669 --> 00:28:30,087
None of this is a lie.

338
00:28:30,587 --> 00:28:33,465
I'll answer any questions
you have for me.

339
00:28:33,882 --> 00:28:36,009
EXTORTION, BLACKMAIL
FALSE ACCUSATION

340
00:28:36,093 --> 00:28:37,302
RAN A STUDENT LOAN SCHEME...

341
00:28:37,386 --> 00:28:38,512
STIRRED UP TROUBLE...

342
00:28:40,431 --> 00:28:42,433
Is this for real, guys?

343
00:28:42,516 --> 00:28:46,270
Baek Ah-jin's shocking past
has been brought to light.

344
00:28:46,353 --> 00:28:49,231
A single post
on a forum is blowing up.

345
00:28:49,314 --> 00:28:51,692
"I'm exposing
who Baek Ah-jin really is.

346
00:28:51,775 --> 00:28:54,695
We were classmates in 11th grade.

347
00:28:54,778 --> 00:28:56,071
She was the devil."

348
00:28:56,155 --> 00:28:58,782
You can tell from the first line
that this is big.

349
00:28:59,450 --> 00:29:00,451
But this is where...

350
00:29:00,534 --> 00:29:02,995
I think I know who this is.
Are you Sim Sung-hee?

351
00:29:03,078 --> 00:29:04,371
Wait, I think I remember her.

352
00:29:04,455 --> 00:29:07,916
She stole stuff and spread rumors,
so she was transferred.

353
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,836
Everyone who grew up in Nojeong-gu
knows who she is.

354
00:29:10,919 --> 00:29:13,172
If you have a conscience,
delete this post.

355
00:29:13,255 --> 00:29:14,715
Wow, she's still at it.

356
00:29:14,798 --> 00:29:18,135
Sung-hee,
you're still the same crazy bitch.

357
00:29:19,553 --> 00:29:21,054
It's not true.

358
00:29:21,430 --> 00:29:23,599
You saw how it was deleted instantly.

359
00:29:23,682 --> 00:29:26,226
I was a model student back in school.

360
00:29:28,270 --> 00:29:31,774
Fine. I'll take your word for it.

361
00:29:33,066 --> 00:29:35,861
Fortunately, it doesn't look like
the media will blow it up.

362
00:29:36,737 --> 00:29:39,782
We'll chalk it up to
some hater acting out.

363
00:29:41,408 --> 00:29:44,411
On the bright side,
I'm receiving positive comments too.

364
00:29:44,495 --> 00:29:45,954
I get a little shy reading them.

365
00:29:48,540 --> 00:29:49,750
You think this is funny?

366
00:29:51,460 --> 00:29:54,713
You're really stressing me out here.

367
00:29:54,797 --> 00:29:58,050
Things like this
could come back to bite you.

368
00:29:58,133 --> 00:30:00,803
And that would be a real headache.

369
00:30:00,886 --> 00:30:02,596
Especially the reporters.

370
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:05,682
Be careful around them, okay?

371
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:08,685
I will. Don't worry.

372
00:30:08,977 --> 00:30:11,855
I'm trusting you on this.

373
00:30:15,651 --> 00:30:17,820
Will you be okay sleeping without me?

374
00:30:17,903 --> 00:30:19,655
Should I ask my grandma to come over?

375
00:30:20,239 --> 00:30:21,532
No, it's fine.

376
00:30:22,157 --> 00:30:24,451
I'll get some sleep
and call you later.

377
00:30:26,787 --> 00:30:29,122
Okay. Sleep tight.

378
00:31:18,463 --> 00:31:19,548
Ah-jin.

379
00:31:25,637 --> 00:31:26,722
Ah-jin.

380
00:31:29,308 --> 00:31:30,517
Ah-jin?

381
00:31:36,023 --> 00:31:37,441
- Ah-jin.
- Ah-jin!

382
00:31:48,368 --> 00:31:49,786
Ah-jin!

383
00:31:53,081 --> 00:31:54,166
Ah-jin.

384
00:31:55,959 --> 00:31:57,044
Ah-jin?

385
00:32:38,377 --> 00:32:40,128
How sick are you?

386
00:32:41,171 --> 00:32:43,715
What brings you here?

387
00:32:46,635 --> 00:32:50,889
You should have told me
if you were sick.

388
00:32:53,266 --> 00:32:54,476
Grandma.

389
00:32:55,435 --> 00:32:59,815
You should've rung the doorbell.
How long were you out there?

390
00:32:59,898 --> 00:33:01,608
Think about yourself right now.

391
00:33:02,734 --> 00:33:06,113
Do I have to hear from In-gang
that you're sick?

392
00:33:07,990 --> 00:33:09,533
It must've been cold out there.

393
00:33:10,993 --> 00:33:13,912
You get used to the cold
when you're old.

394
00:33:18,625 --> 00:33:20,877
You must've been scared, dear.

395
00:33:23,130 --> 00:33:26,174
Being alone
when you're sick is scary.

396
00:33:26,258 --> 00:33:27,259
Come on.

397
00:33:34,474 --> 00:33:36,018
Go on. Eat up.

398
00:33:58,999 --> 00:34:04,337
Once you get better,
let's go get some fresh air.

399
00:34:45,128 --> 00:34:47,214
I fed a stray once.

400
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:53,220
And the next day,
she came back with her kitten.

401
00:34:55,680 --> 00:34:57,933
She must've wanted me to help.

402
00:34:59,267 --> 00:35:01,728
She must've wanted me
to help her kitten.

403
00:35:02,270 --> 00:35:05,315
Even that tiny creature was a mother.

404
00:35:07,484 --> 00:35:09,402
That's just how mothers are.

405
00:35:12,405 --> 00:35:15,117
She's such a pretty little thing.

406
00:35:16,326 --> 00:35:20,205
I'll show her to you someday.

407
00:35:22,124 --> 00:35:23,125
Okay.

408
00:35:28,380 --> 00:35:29,381
Ah-jin.

409
00:35:30,841 --> 00:35:33,844
No matter what happens,
I'm on your side.

410
00:35:35,971 --> 00:35:39,558
Even if everything
they wrote about you was true

411
00:35:40,976 --> 00:35:45,272
I know you must've had your reasons.

412
00:35:48,108 --> 00:35:54,364
I know how gentle and kind you are.

413
00:35:58,785 --> 00:36:00,162
Everyone...

414
00:36:03,331 --> 00:36:05,750
says I'm a bad person.

415
00:36:11,423 --> 00:36:13,633
What am I...

416
00:36:16,011 --> 00:36:17,179
to you?

417
00:36:25,312 --> 00:36:26,688
A gift...

418
00:36:28,982 --> 00:36:32,527
A gift from my daughter.

419
00:36:33,445 --> 00:36:35,447
Just like In-gang and In-mo

420
00:36:36,448 --> 00:36:38,450
you're my child.

421
00:37:08,313 --> 00:37:09,314
Grandma.

422
00:37:09,856 --> 00:37:10,857
Yes?

423
00:37:12,317 --> 00:37:13,693
It's 1-2-2-5.

424
00:37:14,402 --> 00:37:15,779
What do you mean?

425
00:37:17,155 --> 00:37:18,448
It's my door code.

426
00:37:19,866 --> 00:37:22,369
You can come in anytime next time.

427
00:37:22,953 --> 00:37:24,996
Don't wait in the cold
like last night.

428
00:37:25,538 --> 00:37:26,748
It's 1-2-2-5.

429
00:37:27,374 --> 00:37:29,584
That's the day Jesus was born.

430
00:37:29,668 --> 00:37:31,211
He's Buddha's friend.

431
00:38:34,149 --> 00:38:36,192
How did you even get here?

432
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:39,779
I tagged along on your business trip
as a little vacation.

433
00:38:39,863 --> 00:38:43,908
I missed you so much, In-gang.

434
00:38:46,536 --> 00:38:47,537
Hey.

435
00:38:47,912 --> 00:38:50,206
You looked great out there today.

436
00:38:50,290 --> 00:38:52,876
You literally killed it.

437
00:38:53,460 --> 00:38:54,753
I know you better than that.

438
00:38:59,799 --> 00:39:01,593
Why are you really here?

439
00:39:05,597 --> 00:39:08,391
It's about Director Yong's new work.

440
00:39:09,601 --> 00:39:11,853
We need to get back to him
by the end of the week.

441
00:39:11,936 --> 00:39:13,980
When are you going
to give me an answer?

442
00:39:14,064 --> 00:39:15,607
I knew you didn't just drop by.

443
00:39:16,149 --> 00:39:17,317
What's the holdup?

444
00:39:18,068 --> 00:39:20,070
You said you liked the script.

445
00:39:22,322 --> 00:39:23,323
Mi-ri.

446
00:39:23,406 --> 00:39:24,449
Yes?

447
00:39:26,076 --> 00:39:28,453
I'm thinking of doing something else.

448
00:39:28,536 --> 00:39:31,081
Something other
than dramas and movies?

449
00:39:31,164 --> 00:39:33,416
Do you want to be on variety shows?

450
00:39:33,500 --> 00:39:34,709
No, it's not that.

451
00:39:35,293 --> 00:39:36,294
Then what?

452
00:39:38,463 --> 00:39:40,340
Do you think I'm allowed to be happy?

453
00:39:42,300 --> 00:39:43,635
Oh, my goodness.

454
00:39:44,386 --> 00:39:46,429
What are you talking about?

455
00:39:48,014 --> 00:39:50,225
Lately,
I keep finding myself thinking

456
00:39:52,102 --> 00:39:53,853
"I'm happy.

457
00:39:55,605 --> 00:39:57,357
This is what happiness feels like."

458
00:39:57,774 --> 00:40:01,069
Hold on to that feeling
and stay happy at work.

459
00:40:01,569 --> 00:40:03,530
When I'm with Ah-jin

460
00:40:04,906 --> 00:40:06,282
it feels like a dream.

461
00:40:08,076 --> 00:40:09,869
I catch myself smiling for no reason.

462
00:40:11,037 --> 00:40:12,455
People say I've gone mad.

463
00:40:13,998 --> 00:40:15,291
But I'm happy.

464
00:40:16,209 --> 00:40:19,587
I'm so happy that it scares me.

465
00:40:20,630 --> 00:40:23,341
I'm scared that this will end.

466
00:40:24,050 --> 00:40:25,760
I'm afraid I'll be the one...

467
00:40:29,389 --> 00:40:31,099
who destroys this happiness.

468
00:40:40,275 --> 00:40:41,568
Don't tell me you're...

469
00:40:41,985 --> 00:40:44,737
No. Stop jumping to conclusions.

470
00:40:46,656 --> 00:40:49,826
I went to the department store
to buy Ah-jin a birthday gift

471
00:40:49,909 --> 00:40:51,744
and happened to see some baby shoes.

472
00:40:52,495 --> 00:40:53,705
They were so cute.

473
00:40:56,207 --> 00:40:57,625
I didn't even need them

474
00:40:58,501 --> 00:41:01,212
but I couldn't walk away
from these tiny shoes.

475
00:41:01,713 --> 00:41:02,797
So I bought them.

476
00:41:09,387 --> 00:41:11,931
Are you considering marrying Ah-jin?

477
00:41:16,686 --> 00:41:18,229
Does she want to marry you?

478
00:41:20,565 --> 00:41:21,566
I'm not sure.

479
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:25,653
I hope she does.

480
00:41:29,073 --> 00:41:30,492
Look how small it is.

481
00:41:48,718 --> 00:41:49,719
Ah-jin.

482
00:42:11,366 --> 00:42:12,450
You seem surprised.

483
00:42:14,702 --> 00:42:17,247
No, I'm glad to see you.

484
00:42:22,168 --> 00:42:23,670
When did you get out?

485
00:42:24,003 --> 00:42:25,255
Not long ago.

486
00:42:26,631 --> 00:42:28,383
I was released sooner than expected.

487
00:42:33,846 --> 00:42:35,723
You look healthy.

488
00:42:42,313 --> 00:42:43,815
Are you at peace now?

489
00:42:45,567 --> 00:42:47,986
Yes, a little.

490
00:42:48,069 --> 00:42:49,862
And you got what you wanted?

491
00:42:55,451 --> 00:42:56,869
All thanks to you.

492
00:42:59,664 --> 00:43:01,165
And how do you think I am?

493
00:43:03,459 --> 00:43:05,086
You're a good person.

494
00:43:07,547 --> 00:43:09,757
I'm sure you can make it
through anything.

495
00:43:10,675 --> 00:43:11,801
"Good person"?

496
00:43:14,345 --> 00:43:16,639
How long do you think
I can stay that way?

497
00:43:21,644 --> 00:43:22,812
Look who it is!

498
00:43:23,688 --> 00:43:25,064
Jung-ho, is that you?

499
00:43:26,107 --> 00:43:27,317
What brings you here?

500
00:43:27,859 --> 00:43:31,904
You told me it was a beautiful temple
and said that I should stop by.

501
00:43:32,196 --> 00:43:33,197
How have you been?

502
00:43:33,573 --> 00:43:34,991
When did you get out?

503
00:43:35,074 --> 00:43:36,200
A couple of weeks ago.

504
00:43:37,118 --> 00:43:39,537
Goodness. You went through so much.

505
00:43:40,455 --> 00:43:42,457
This is my grandson.

506
00:43:43,499 --> 00:43:47,170
And she's
my older grandson's girlfriend.

507
00:43:47,253 --> 00:43:49,881
Ma'am, we've already met.

508
00:43:49,964 --> 00:43:51,799
You two know each other?

509
00:43:53,134 --> 00:43:54,135
Yes.

510
00:43:54,218 --> 00:43:57,305
I had to make ends meet
after graduating from high school

511
00:43:57,388 --> 00:43:59,098
and he helped me out a lot.

512
00:43:59,182 --> 00:44:00,183
I see.

513
00:44:00,892 --> 00:44:04,020
And I worked part-time
at his café for a year.

514
00:44:08,191 --> 00:44:11,110
How do you know Mrs. Hong?

515
00:44:12,111 --> 00:44:16,991
Well, we met at a temple...

516
00:44:17,075 --> 00:44:18,284
She came

517
00:44:19,869 --> 00:44:22,038
to volunteer at the prison I was in.

518
00:44:25,792 --> 00:44:28,336
Ma'am, I'll see you again soon.

519
00:44:29,003 --> 00:44:31,297
I've always wanted to buy you a meal.

520
00:44:31,381 --> 00:44:33,508
I'd love that.

521
00:44:33,591 --> 00:44:35,385
Hold on.

522
00:44:36,386 --> 00:44:38,179
- Give me your number.
- Sure.

523
00:44:42,141 --> 00:44:43,267
Here you go.

524
00:44:43,351 --> 00:44:45,853
I really hope we meet again.

525
00:44:46,604 --> 00:44:48,856
What a small world, you and Ah-jin.

526
00:45:14,257 --> 00:45:15,717
He still hasn't come home?

527
00:45:18,886 --> 00:45:19,887
You're home.

528
00:45:20,471 --> 00:45:21,806
What took you so long?

529
00:45:22,390 --> 00:45:23,891
I missed you like crazy.

530
00:45:34,360 --> 00:45:35,820
Who are you?

531
00:45:44,245 --> 00:45:45,288
Who are you?

532
00:45:45,371 --> 00:45:47,081
Why did you barge into
someone else's home?

533
00:45:47,165 --> 00:45:49,083
Exactly! What are you doing
in someone else's house?

534
00:45:50,293 --> 00:45:52,670
- What a pervert.
- "Pervert"?

535
00:45:53,045 --> 00:45:54,380
Why did you hug me?

536
00:45:54,464 --> 00:45:56,591
You hugged me from behind!

537
00:45:56,674 --> 00:45:57,800
Unbelievable.

538
00:46:04,974 --> 00:46:05,975
Seriously.

539
00:46:06,893 --> 00:46:10,438
You hide in a man's house
and hug him.

540
00:46:11,105 --> 00:46:13,816
Check his face first
if you're going to hug him.

541
00:46:14,901 --> 00:46:17,445
I don't let just anyone
touch my body.

542
00:46:20,448 --> 00:46:22,950
Did I steal a kiss
or take your pants off?

543
00:46:23,785 --> 00:46:26,078
All I did was hug you from behind.

544
00:46:26,162 --> 00:46:27,413
I'm the one who's offended.

545
00:46:27,872 --> 00:46:29,332
But I'm the victim.

546
00:46:32,627 --> 00:46:34,504
Jun-seo, that inconsiderate jerk.

547
00:46:35,004 --> 00:46:36,756
He should have warned me.

548
00:46:37,131 --> 00:46:39,050
Guess he doesn't
tell you much either.

549
00:46:42,470 --> 00:46:43,805
Let me ask you something.

550
00:46:44,722 --> 00:46:45,973
What are you two?

551
00:46:49,101 --> 00:46:51,229
You know what? Never mind.

552
00:46:51,312 --> 00:46:52,647
I don't even have to ask.

553
00:46:53,147 --> 00:46:55,566
You wait for him at home and hug him.

554
00:46:56,150 --> 00:46:57,360
That says it all.

555
00:46:58,361 --> 00:46:59,362
I'm out.

556
00:46:59,695 --> 00:47:00,905
What's your name?

557
00:47:03,616 --> 00:47:04,617
Why do you ask?

558
00:47:04,992 --> 00:47:09,956
We may be strangers,
but we did share a hug.

559
00:47:10,331 --> 00:47:13,251
- Excuse me?
- I've never met his friend before.

560
00:47:14,544 --> 00:47:18,381
I didn't know he had any friends,
so I figured I should get your name.

561
00:47:18,756 --> 00:47:20,091
Ask him yourself.

562
00:47:26,681 --> 00:47:28,683
Haven't we met before, though?

563
00:47:28,975 --> 00:47:31,352
Not "we". You must've seen me.

564
00:47:32,061 --> 00:47:33,062
On TV.

565
00:47:34,313 --> 00:47:35,314
TV?

566
00:47:39,235 --> 00:47:40,444
Right?

567
00:47:40,528 --> 00:47:41,654
The celebrity!

568
00:47:42,071 --> 00:47:44,156
The has-been--

569
00:47:51,664 --> 00:47:52,665
Sorry.

570
00:48:09,891 --> 00:48:11,100
Hey, boss!

571
00:48:12,226 --> 00:48:13,394
Is it really you?

572
00:48:14,145 --> 00:48:16,272
It's been a while, Jae-oh.

573
00:48:18,024 --> 00:48:19,150
Is something wrong?

574
00:48:19,942 --> 00:48:22,236
No. Not yet.

575
00:48:24,447 --> 00:48:26,449
What is it? You can tell me.

576
00:48:29,201 --> 00:48:30,202
Okay.

577
00:48:32,079 --> 00:48:33,080
All right.

578
00:48:34,081 --> 00:48:36,000
Send me his info
as soon as you get it.

579
00:48:37,126 --> 00:48:38,127
All right.

580
00:48:54,477 --> 00:48:55,645
Did Ah-jin call you?

581
00:48:57,188 --> 00:48:58,356
How did you know?

582
00:48:59,148 --> 00:49:01,984
You make a certain face
when you talk to her.

583
00:49:02,443 --> 00:49:03,486
What face?

584
00:49:05,863 --> 00:49:07,531
That's a face I want to punch.

585
00:49:07,615 --> 00:49:08,824
Imagine how I felt.

586
00:49:13,788 --> 00:49:15,665
If she's calling me

587
00:49:17,375 --> 00:49:19,085
that means something's up.

588
00:49:19,669 --> 00:49:21,128
Something doesn't feel right.

589
00:49:21,587 --> 00:49:22,964
How did she sound?

590
00:49:23,464 --> 00:49:25,883
More depressed than usual.

591
00:49:29,387 --> 00:49:30,596
Maybe I'm mistaken.

592
00:49:33,933 --> 00:49:35,393
What did she want?

593
00:49:37,603 --> 00:49:39,522
She told me not to tell you.

594
00:49:44,944 --> 00:49:47,780
Also, don't go home tonight.

595
00:49:48,072 --> 00:49:49,240
There's a crazy girl.

596
00:50:14,181 --> 00:50:18,644
There's good news shaking
both the literary and film worlds.

597
00:50:18,728 --> 00:50:20,813
A bestselling novel
that stirred major buzz

598
00:50:20,896 --> 00:50:23,274
is finally headed to the big screen.

599
00:50:23,357 --> 00:50:26,068
Author Yoon Seok-ha,
winner of the Ennoble Literary Award

600
00:50:26,152 --> 00:50:28,195
has announced that his latest work,
Winter Sleep

601
00:50:28,279 --> 00:50:30,072
is being adapted into a film.

602
00:50:30,156 --> 00:50:32,533
Winter Sleep is a novel
about a man and a woman

603
00:50:32,616 --> 00:50:34,618
who reunite after parting ways

604
00:50:34,702 --> 00:50:39,874
slowly healing their past wounds
and rebuilding their love together.

605
00:50:39,957 --> 00:50:43,627
Meanwhile, Yoon Seok-ha was spotted
on a date with actress Lena

606
00:50:43,711 --> 00:50:45,254
sparking romance rumors.

607
00:50:45,337 --> 00:50:48,007
With Lena's name being mentioned
as the heroine of Winter Sleep

608
00:50:48,090 --> 00:50:50,968
the online communities
are buzzing with speculation.

609
00:50:52,845 --> 00:50:54,555
CEO YOON JUN-SEO

610
00:51:08,611 --> 00:51:11,322
You're Mr. Yoon Jun-seo, right?

611
00:51:12,698 --> 00:51:13,991
Do you know me?

612
00:51:15,826 --> 00:51:19,497
We haven't met,
but I know enough about you.

613
00:51:26,337 --> 00:51:28,672
It's surprising enough that you,
the author of Winter Sleep

614
00:51:28,756 --> 00:51:32,218
had been an anonymous investor
in Longstar for the past year.

615
00:51:32,676 --> 00:51:36,097
But it turns out you were
Ah-jin's secret benefactor too.

616
00:51:38,099 --> 00:51:39,266
Is Ah-jin doing okay?

617
00:51:39,809 --> 00:51:41,644
So you haven't seen her lately?

618
00:51:41,727 --> 00:51:44,355
Are you curious
about her and In-gang?

619
00:51:44,605 --> 00:51:47,108
I just want her happy.

620
00:51:47,483 --> 00:51:52,571
She's confident and ambitious.
And she's loaded with talent.

621
00:51:52,655 --> 00:51:55,282
When she wants something,
she goes straight for it.

622
00:51:55,366 --> 00:51:58,244
And she can be mesmerizing
when needed.

623
00:51:58,327 --> 00:52:00,579
Is actor Heo In-gang okay?

624
00:52:02,498 --> 00:52:04,708
Thanks for asking about him too.

625
00:52:06,085 --> 00:52:10,714
I was worried myself,
but he's happier than ever.

626
00:52:13,926 --> 00:52:17,221
In-gang isn't just one of our actors.

627
00:52:17,304 --> 00:52:19,515
He's like a brother
I deeply care about.

628
00:52:19,974 --> 00:52:23,769
I would never let anything
make him unhappy.

629
00:52:24,353 --> 00:52:26,814
I would never let anything
make Ah-jin unhappy, either.

630
00:52:26,897 --> 00:52:29,191
You also need to honor
the contract terms.

631
00:52:29,942 --> 00:52:30,943
We will.

632
00:52:33,154 --> 00:52:35,364
Ah-jin's burnt out,
even if she won't say it.

633
00:52:35,447 --> 00:52:36,866
She needs rest.

634
00:52:37,241 --> 00:52:39,076
She's in her mid-20s.

635
00:52:39,160 --> 00:52:41,370
She should be working, not resting.

636
00:52:42,037 --> 00:52:43,998
It's not about age.

637
00:52:44,415 --> 00:52:46,709
Don't tell me you're
seriously considering marrying her.

638
00:52:48,085 --> 00:52:50,713
She has a big future ahead of her.

639
00:52:51,213 --> 00:52:53,215
Don't think about tying her down.

640
00:52:53,841 --> 00:52:56,510
Why does it have to be her
for that show?

641
00:52:57,219 --> 00:52:59,263
That was the author's condition.

642
00:52:59,346 --> 00:53:01,849
Studios are desperate
to adapt Winter Sleep

643
00:53:01,932 --> 00:53:04,268
so the competition was fierce.

644
00:53:04,727 --> 00:53:08,480
What let our company win the bid
was exactly that condition.

645
00:53:10,900 --> 00:53:12,735
This is hard, In-gang.

646
00:53:13,777 --> 00:53:14,778
Let's talk later.

647
00:53:26,457 --> 00:53:27,541
Author Yoon Seok-ha?

648
00:53:28,584 --> 00:53:29,585
What about him?

649
00:53:30,169 --> 00:53:31,170
You didn't see the news?

650
00:53:32,129 --> 00:53:33,672
They say he's dating Lena.

651
00:53:33,756 --> 00:53:35,549
Really? Good for them.

652
00:53:38,219 --> 00:53:43,265
He's insisting that you star
in the drama adaptation of his work.

653
00:53:45,351 --> 00:53:47,353
That was his condition
for investing in our company.

654
00:53:49,271 --> 00:53:50,272
I heard.

655
00:53:52,358 --> 00:53:53,359
You knew?

656
00:53:53,692 --> 00:53:55,402
The script was decent.

657
00:53:55,986 --> 00:53:58,113
So I told him
I'd discuss it with you.

658
00:53:58,864 --> 00:54:01,867
It seems that Ms. Seo
really wants me to do it.

659
00:54:02,660 --> 00:54:03,869
What do you think?

660
00:54:05,913 --> 00:54:09,458
Let's think it over for one week.

661
00:54:10,125 --> 00:54:11,126
Okay.

662
00:54:40,364 --> 00:54:41,365
You're late.

663
00:54:45,077 --> 00:54:46,120
You're the one who's late.

664
00:54:47,037 --> 00:54:48,706
It's been over a year.

665
00:54:49,206 --> 00:54:52,543
You promised you'd come back.

666
00:54:55,838 --> 00:54:57,881
Congratulations, you pulled it off.

667
00:55:00,718 --> 00:55:03,929
You blackmailed Ms. Seo with money,
poked at In-gang

668
00:55:04,013 --> 00:55:05,639
and made me come to you.

669
00:55:07,808 --> 00:55:08,809
I'm impressed.

670
00:55:09,268 --> 00:55:11,395
You're the one making me this way.

671
00:55:14,273 --> 00:55:15,649
Ms. Seo told me.

672
00:55:17,901 --> 00:55:18,944
Why?

673
00:55:20,696 --> 00:55:21,864
I wanted to help you.

674
00:55:23,240 --> 00:55:25,034
That's my duty, isn't it?

675
00:55:27,161 --> 00:55:28,162
It always has been.

676
00:55:28,245 --> 00:55:31,206
- What do you want me to do?
- That's my question.

677
00:55:32,583 --> 00:55:34,918
Isn't it time to end it with In-gang?

678
00:55:35,961 --> 00:55:36,962
Why?

679
00:55:38,756 --> 00:55:40,466
Did you actually
fall in love with him?

680
00:55:49,892 --> 00:55:50,893
What about you?

681
00:55:52,102 --> 00:55:55,022
I heard you were dating Lena.

682
00:55:55,439 --> 00:55:56,440
Yes.

683
00:55:57,316 --> 00:55:58,317
Why?

684
00:55:59,109 --> 00:56:01,528
- Does it bother you?
- She used to torment me.

685
00:56:02,279 --> 00:56:03,947
You don't know what she'll pull.

686
00:56:04,031 --> 00:56:05,991
All the more reason
to keep her close.

687
00:56:06,075 --> 00:56:08,660
So I can stop her
from getting to you.

688
00:56:14,500 --> 00:56:15,959
Something's different

689
00:56:17,252 --> 00:56:18,253
about you.

690
00:56:19,505 --> 00:56:20,589
People...

691
00:56:25,302 --> 00:56:26,387
change.

692
00:56:41,527 --> 00:56:42,653
You didn't eat, right?

693
00:56:48,909 --> 00:56:50,119
Hi, Lena.

694
00:56:52,162 --> 00:56:53,247
Why are you here?

695
00:56:55,290 --> 00:56:56,458
Explain.

696
00:56:56,542 --> 00:56:58,877
- We were talking.
- "Talking"?

697
00:56:58,961 --> 00:57:01,547
Then, do it outside, not here.

698
00:57:02,089 --> 00:57:05,592
Does In-gang know you're here?

699
00:57:06,468 --> 00:57:07,469
Actually...

700
00:57:07,970 --> 00:57:11,014
Can you two
even make your relationship public?

701
00:57:14,143 --> 00:57:15,227
Do as you please.

702
00:57:15,853 --> 00:57:16,854
Hey.

703
00:57:16,937 --> 00:57:18,939
You think I won't?

704
00:57:19,022 --> 00:57:21,316
Let go! This is so wrong!

705
00:57:26,822 --> 00:57:28,240
I tailed him for a few days.

706
00:57:28,323 --> 00:57:31,034
He went to pay respects to your dad.
He cried and apologized.

707
00:57:31,785 --> 00:57:32,995
He still hasn't changed.

708
00:57:33,662 --> 00:57:34,663
Is that all?

709
00:57:34,746 --> 00:57:37,583
He usually does volunteer work
in the afternoon and goes home.

710
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:40,043
He doesn't drink or meet his friends.

711
00:57:40,127 --> 00:57:42,671
When there's no volunteer work,
he goes to the gym

712
00:57:43,255 --> 00:57:44,673
or reads at a café.

713
00:57:45,716 --> 00:57:47,050
I don't think you need to worry.

714
00:57:48,260 --> 00:57:49,261
Okay.

715
00:57:55,142 --> 00:57:56,226
Is dating fun?

716
00:57:57,603 --> 00:57:58,604
Why do you ask?

717
00:58:01,064 --> 00:58:02,065
Because it looks like it.

718
00:58:02,858 --> 00:58:04,067
You don't call me

719
00:58:05,861 --> 00:58:07,029
because you're doing well.

720
00:58:08,363 --> 00:58:11,200
Yes, I'm doing well. I'm happy.

721
00:58:23,378 --> 00:58:24,963
Did you look into
that exposé about Ah-jin?

722
00:58:25,255 --> 00:58:26,256
How did it go?

723
00:58:26,340 --> 00:58:28,967
It was deleted
an hour after it was posted.

724
00:58:29,051 --> 00:58:30,677
And the source is unverified.

725
00:58:31,011 --> 00:58:32,471
"Can't and won't."

726
00:58:33,639 --> 00:58:35,641
You think I pay you to hear that?

727
00:58:36,016 --> 00:58:38,352
When did I ever say
that I can't or won't?

728
00:58:39,228 --> 00:58:41,313
Give me some time. I'm still digging.

729
00:58:43,482 --> 00:58:44,483
Dong-gyu, it's me.

730
00:58:45,192 --> 00:58:46,193
Lena.

731
00:58:46,944 --> 00:58:49,905
Do you know
where In-gang is right now?

732
00:58:57,913 --> 00:58:58,914
Where are we going?

733
00:59:00,123 --> 00:59:02,626
You'll see. It'll be fun.

734
00:59:20,269 --> 00:59:21,770
Happy birthday, Ah-jin.

735
00:59:22,312 --> 00:59:23,313
Thanks.

736
00:59:40,372 --> 00:59:43,166
This might be cringe

737
00:59:44,167 --> 00:59:45,836
so please don't laugh.

738
00:59:46,962 --> 00:59:48,046
What's it about?

739
00:59:49,172 --> 00:59:50,173
Go on.

740
00:59:56,179 --> 00:59:57,723
I'm so grateful

741
00:59:59,308 --> 01:00:00,559
you were born

742
01:00:01,643 --> 01:00:03,562
and that you came into my life.

743
01:00:07,357 --> 01:00:10,694
It's been a year,
and when I'm with you

744
01:00:12,529 --> 01:00:13,614
my heart still races.

745
01:00:14,781 --> 01:00:20,454
This might be sudden,
but I hope you won't say no.

746
01:00:24,750 --> 01:00:27,586
They must have told me
the wrong floor.

747
01:00:31,882 --> 01:00:32,883
In-gang.

748
01:00:34,134 --> 01:00:36,845
What are you doing here with Ah-jin?

749
01:00:40,390 --> 01:00:42,309
- Can't you tell?
- A date?

750
01:00:42,392 --> 01:00:43,894
Oh, it's your birthday.

751
01:00:45,604 --> 01:00:47,189
Happy birthday.

752
01:00:49,608 --> 01:00:51,526
I'm also here on a date.

753
01:00:52,110 --> 01:00:54,529
Since we're all here,
why don't we celebrate together?

754
01:00:55,906 --> 01:00:57,616
Is that okay, Jun-seo?

755
01:01:02,204 --> 01:01:03,664
Mind if I sit?

756
01:01:04,498 --> 01:01:05,707
Take a seat, Jun-seo.

757
01:01:23,225 --> 01:01:27,854
That's right. I heard you two
used to be classmates.

758
01:01:29,022 --> 01:01:30,774
We live in such a small world.

759
01:01:31,817 --> 01:01:33,110
What a coincidence.

760
01:01:35,612 --> 01:01:36,613
Classmates?

761
01:01:38,532 --> 01:01:39,908
Technically

762
01:01:40,992 --> 01:01:42,285
we were siblings.

763
01:01:42,369 --> 01:01:45,288
Our parents remarried
when we were young.

764
01:01:49,710 --> 01:01:52,379
It's not exactly my favorite memory.

765
01:01:53,755 --> 01:01:54,756
Yeah?

766
01:01:55,340 --> 01:01:56,341
Why?

767
01:01:57,509 --> 01:02:02,556
My mother didn't treat her
so well back then.

768
01:02:04,057 --> 01:02:05,642
Because of that

769
01:02:06,810 --> 01:02:09,604
I still feel guilty

770
01:02:09,980 --> 01:02:13,024
and am willing to do
anything for her.

771
01:02:13,900 --> 01:02:15,068
You don't have to.

772
01:02:15,819 --> 01:02:17,154
I've gotten over it.

773
01:02:20,615 --> 01:02:21,616
I'm fine.

774
01:02:23,118 --> 01:02:24,119
You're right.

775
01:02:26,455 --> 01:02:28,457
You look fine. I'm happy for you.

776
01:02:30,584 --> 01:02:31,668
Happy birthday.

777
01:02:39,676 --> 01:02:41,762
I should congratulate
you two as well.

778
01:02:41,845 --> 01:02:43,263
We're just friends.

779
01:02:47,309 --> 01:02:48,310
He's right.

780
01:02:50,520 --> 01:02:52,063
We're only using each other.

781
01:02:55,358 --> 01:02:59,237
By the way, why did you come
to Jun-seo's place the other night?

782
01:02:59,821 --> 01:03:01,281
It was so late at night.

783
01:03:01,865 --> 01:03:03,408
You really scared me.

784
01:03:04,117 --> 01:03:05,202
That was

785
01:03:06,828 --> 01:03:08,121
because

786
01:03:09,080 --> 01:03:12,959
I wanted to politely turn down
Winter Sleep.

787
01:03:16,546 --> 01:03:17,547
What's wrong?

788
01:03:18,715 --> 01:03:21,259
How do you tell such a blatant lie
with a smile on your face?

789
01:03:22,219 --> 01:03:25,514
That was not the vibe
I picked up from them.

790
01:03:28,225 --> 01:03:29,726
It's her birthday.

791
01:03:30,769 --> 01:03:33,146
Take it down a notch.
We're here to celebrate.

792
01:03:37,776 --> 01:03:39,110
You'll have to excuse us.

793
01:03:55,836 --> 01:03:58,088
I want you to be straight with me.

794
01:03:59,214 --> 01:04:00,382
Is it me or Ah-jin?

795
01:04:01,299 --> 01:04:02,843
Do you even want to help me?

796
01:04:03,426 --> 01:04:04,845
Whatever you do

797
01:04:05,929 --> 01:04:08,306
- In-gang won't go back to you.
- I know that.

798
01:04:08,390 --> 01:04:09,975
You think I'm doing this
to win him back?

799
01:04:10,517 --> 01:04:14,062
Why her, though,
out of all the women?

800
01:04:15,063 --> 01:04:16,439
There's something wrong with her.

801
01:04:17,023 --> 01:04:19,109
Didn't you see how brazen she was

802
01:04:19,192 --> 01:04:21,444
when her relationship
with you was exposed?

803
01:04:21,778 --> 01:04:24,698
She's a really bad person.

804
01:04:24,781 --> 01:04:26,449
Do you really not see it?

805
01:04:26,533 --> 01:04:29,703
Why does no one see it but me?

806
01:04:54,394 --> 01:04:55,896
Oh, dear.

807
01:05:29,930 --> 01:05:32,766
Are you two really siblings?

808
01:05:33,934 --> 01:05:34,935
Yes.

809
01:05:35,685 --> 01:05:36,686
We were.

810
01:05:37,520 --> 01:05:38,772
Why didn't you tell me?

811
01:05:42,859 --> 01:05:45,654
I didn't tell you
because you never asked.

812
01:05:46,738 --> 01:05:48,573
You can ask me anything.

813
01:05:49,115 --> 01:05:50,241
I'll answer.

814
01:05:56,164 --> 01:05:57,415
Just siblings?

815
01:05:58,375 --> 01:05:59,542
Not anymore.

816
01:06:01,127 --> 01:06:03,296
Our parents got divorced.

817
01:06:04,881 --> 01:06:05,882
I'm sorry.

818
01:06:08,343 --> 01:06:09,594
For what?

819
01:06:11,763 --> 01:06:12,764
One second.

820
01:06:15,266 --> 01:06:16,851
Hey, In-mo. What's up?

821
01:06:21,022 --> 01:06:22,023
What?

822
01:06:23,316 --> 01:06:24,401
She found it?

823
01:06:26,069 --> 01:06:27,070
What is it?

824
01:06:27,529 --> 01:06:29,739
My grandma found the notebook
she lost last year.

825
01:06:32,325 --> 01:06:33,410
She did?

826
01:06:34,452 --> 01:06:35,453
Okay.

827
01:06:36,287 --> 01:06:37,288
All right.

828
01:06:40,500 --> 01:06:42,085
The notebook?

829
01:06:42,752 --> 01:06:46,673
She used to write in it like a diary,
but she lost it last year.

830
01:06:47,257 --> 01:06:48,258
She found that.

831
01:06:49,801 --> 01:06:52,512
She went to your place
to cook a birthday meal for you

832
01:06:52,595 --> 01:06:55,807
but now she's lying down
and hasn't eaten anything.

833
01:06:56,474 --> 01:07:00,437
In-mo's out of town, so she's alone.
And I have to catch a flight tonight.

834
01:07:04,357 --> 01:07:05,358
Ah-jin.

835
01:07:06,568 --> 01:07:08,028
Can you check on her for me?

836
01:07:17,829 --> 01:07:19,998
It feels like we crashed
your birthday party.

837
01:07:22,333 --> 01:07:23,334
Ah-jin.

838
01:07:25,086 --> 01:07:26,421
Happy birthday.

839
01:07:27,505 --> 01:07:30,050
We'll head out. Have a great time.

840
01:08:02,248 --> 01:08:03,583
It's 1-2-2-5.

841
01:08:04,417 --> 01:08:06,753
You can come in anytime next time.

842
01:08:52,841 --> 01:08:53,925
Wait out here.

843
01:09:58,531 --> 01:09:59,532
You're here.

844
01:10:22,055 --> 01:10:23,056
How did it go?

845
01:10:23,806 --> 01:10:24,807
Nothing yet.

846
01:10:41,616 --> 01:10:42,617
Ah-jin.

847
01:12:04,907 --> 01:12:09,329
DEAR X

848
01:14:28,843 --> 01:14:30,845
Subtitles by Ho-young Yun

